{
    "SchemaVersion": 1,
    "Name": "Iron Channel",
    "Description": "The v0.1 map. One island cut in two by an east-west channel, with three ways over it: a causeway in the middle that nobody can take away, and a bridge on each flank that anybody can. Blowing both bridges funnels the whole match through the middle; it can never strand a jeep, which is the one thing that would make a match unwinnable. Bunkers face each other down the centre line at 140 m. Each side's two towers stand 36 m apart, more than twice the 10 m reveal radius, so one drive cannot confirm both. Everything is placed in pairs rotated 180 degrees about the origin: neither side has a shorter run to the other's flag. Land is always at y = 0 - the whole game is resolved on that one plane - so the only relief on the map is the 0.7 m bank down to the water, and driving off one drowns you.",
